# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# GlassWorm toolkit — .gitignore
#
# Keep the TOOLS in git. Keep the FINDINGS out.
# Scan output names your orgs, repos, branches and infected paths — a map of
# your attack surface. It is also regenerated by any scan, so there is no
# reason to version it.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Scan output and findings (regenerate with the scanners any time)
reports/
*.log
findings*
infected*
auditlog-*.json
*.sarif

# Scan data files, but KEEP the shipped IOC list the scanners depend on
*.tsv
!data/compromised-extensions.tsv

# Recovered malware samples / payload analysis — never commit these
payload*
samples/
quarantine/

# Mirror clones and purge working dirs
*-purge.git/
gw-purge*/
*.mirror/

# Local overrides a teammate may add
*.local
*.local.sh
config.local

# Editor / OS noise
.DS_Store
.idea/
*.swp
*~

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Deliberately tracked: scan-*.sh, fix-local.sh, clean-commit.sh,
# purge-history.sh, check-extensions.sh, automation/, data/, iocs.txt, *.md
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
